what are the allowed image types for astro

In Astro, the commonly allowed/usable image types are:

Standard image formats
These work in normal HTML like <img> and generally in Astro:

.png
.jpg / .jpeg
.gif
.webp
.avif
.svg
With Astro’s image pipeline (astro:assets)
Astro best supports:

JPEG
PNG
WebP
AVIF
SVG as a source file, though SVG handling is a bit different because it’s already vector
Typical usage:

Copy
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import myImage from '../assets/photo.png';
---

<Image src={myImage} alt="Example" />
Public folder images
If placed in /public, you can use basically any browser-supported image format directly:

Copy
<img src="/images/logo.svg" alt="Logo" />
Notes
SVG is great for logos/icons
WebP and AVIF are best for performance
GIF works, but for animation it’s often better to use WebM or MP4
ICO is usually used for favicons, not regular content images
Practical recommendation
For your logo in Astro:

use logo.svg if it’s vector
use logo.webp or logo.png if it’s raster
Good choices by use case
Logo: SVG
Photos: WebP / AVIF / JPEG
Transparent graphics: PNG / WebP / SVG
Icons: SVG
Favicon: ICO, PNG, or SVG depending on setup
